# Who owns what, and why this file exists.
#
# Two agents work this repository in parallel, on acquisition and on the
# student product. For a while the boundary was described as "SEO" and
# "Alexi", which stopped being true the moment growth work began reaching
# into the recommendation engine - and that is where things started
# colliding. So the split is drawn at files, which cannot drift.
#
# GitHub uses this to request reviews. Its more useful job here is to make
# the boundary visible on every pull request rather than remembered.
#
# Editing a file you do not own is not forbidden. Saying so in the pull
# request description, rather than discovering it in a merge, is the ask.

